WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.950
Logging and CISA
telemetry are where branch

2
00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:05.850
modernization most often
goes wrong quietly.

3
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:13.800
M-26-14 rescinded M-21-31 on May 22, 2026.

4
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:18.067
Logs must be searchable for six
months and retrievable for a year,

5
00:00:18.067 --> 00:00:22.650
and agencies must be able to show
addresses, ports and session details.

6
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:26.075
A branch with nothing at its edge
doesn't produce that record.

7
00:00:26.075 --> 00:00:29.047
When branches leave the
managed TIC service,

8
00:00:29.047 --> 00:00:32.100
the telemetry CISA has
been receiving stops.

9
00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.825
The replacement is CLAW, CISA's
log aggregation warehouse,

10
00:00:35.825 --> 00:00:40.463
and onboarding takes the agency, CISA
and the provider working together.

11
00:00:40.463 --> 00:00:44.106
That's a three-party dependency
with its own lead time,

12
00:00:44.106 --> 00:00:47.749
so it belongs on the critical
path, starting in Phase 0.

13
00:00:47.749 --> 00:00:48.950
Here's the decision.

14
00:00:48.950 --> 00:00:53.941
The exit criterion for leaving MTIPS,
and for ending each branch's MPLS,

15
00:00:53.941 --> 00:00:57.125
is confirmed CLAW parity,
not branch cutover.

16
00:00:57.125 --> 00:01:01.250
Cutting circuits first trades a
transport gap for a visibility gap.

17
00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:03.987
Ownership splits three ways on purpose.

18
00:01:03.987 --> 00:01:06.737
The CISO decides when parity is reached.

19
00:01:06.737 --> 00:01:10.362
Security operations confirms
it, branch by branch.

20
00:01:10.362 --> 00:01:13.747
And only a contracting officer
can terminate a contract,

21
00:01:13.747 --> 00:01:18.212
so the contracting officer ends the
circuit, only after that confirmation.

22
00:01:18.212 --> 00:01:22.213
No engineer can cancel a circuit,
however redundant it looks.

23
00:01:22.213 --> 00:01:24.070
Next, the long interim.
